===Etymology===
From {{etyl|it}} {{term|balcone|lang=it}} "balcony, floor-length window" from Old {{etyl|it|-}}, of Persian origin "''بالاخانه''" '''Bālākhāneh''' or its variant '''Bālākhouneh''', the elevated platform projecting from the side of a building, smaller than and different from "terrace" that adjoins the yard. Although today it is common to call it '''Bālākon''' in Persian, '''Bālākhāneh''' is a compound word like many other words in (standard) Persian. It is consisted of '''Bālā''', means "up" + '''Khāneh''' means "house", usually called '''Khouneh''' in everyday conversation and there is a different word in Persian for exterior upper covering of a building, the "roof" and It is '''Bām''' (''بام'').
There are many words that different cultures borrowed from each other and it is a natural phenomenon. But there are a lot of words came from Persian and any other Iranian languages in Europian languages and semitic ones that many do not know where its origin is or mostly supposed that they are Arabic wrongly. It is because of the Arabs invasion to Iran and their kind of strong autocratic apartheid or dictatorial control which people of Iran could not speak and write in their own languages officially and even they were not ellowed to name their children Iranian names. Well, there are a lot things that arabs even did not know anything about them. Hence, those things had to be Arabicised as a word to release and then because of the international exchanges of varied cultures they have come to the other languages in the form was forced to.

